    <code code="51848-0" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation note"/>
    <title>Assessment</title>
    <text><list><item>Invasive ductal carcinoma of the upper outer quadrant of the right breast, stage IA (pT1c pN0(sn) M0), grade 2, estrogen and progesterone receptor positive, HER2 negative, recurrence score 14; treated by right total mastectomy with sentinel node biopsy and on adjuvant tamoxifen; synthetic modern counterpart of the documented 1931 breast cancer and mastectomy: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Estrogen receptor positive status of the breast cancer (ER 90 percent, PR 60 percent): active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Absence of the right breast after mastectomy with flat closure; she chose not to have reconstruction and not to wear an external prosthesis: active, confirmed [S]</item><item>Long-term use of tamoxifen as adjuvant endocrine therapy: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

  </section>
