<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.10" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="18776-5" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Plan of care note"/>
    <title>Plan of Treatment</title>
    <text><list><item>Medical oncology consultation to confirm the adjuvant endocrine therapy plan, advise on hot flashes, set the surveillance plan, and advise on genetic assessment. Guideline: NCCN Clinical Practice Guidelines in Oncology: Breast Cancer, Version 5.2025 (2025); Adjuvant Endocrine Therapy for Women With Hormone Receptor-Positive Breast Cancer: ASCO Clinical Practice Guideline Focused Update (2019) [S]</item><item>Tamoxifen 20 mg daily for at least five years, with questions at every visit about hot flashes, abnormal vaginal bleeding, and leg swelling or breathlessness, and a yearly gynecologic assessment. Guideline: Adjuvant Endocrine Therapy for Women With Hormone Receptor-Positive Breast Cancer: ASCO Clinical Practice Guideline Focused Update (2019); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Lymphedema risk counseling and arm checks at every visit; bone health by calcium and vitamin D from diet and weight-bearing exercise; distress, depression, and anxiety screening at intervals. Guideline: American Cancer Society/American Society of Clinical Oncology Breast Cancer Survivorship Care Guideline. CA Cancer J Clin 2016;66(1):43-73 (2016); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item><item>Written survivorship care plan, at least 150 minutes of activity a week, alcohol at or below one drink a day, and her decisions about reconstruction and a prosthesis recorded and respected. Guideline: American Cancer Society/American Society of Clinical Oncology Breast Cancer Survivorship Care Guideline. CA Cancer J Clin 2016;66(1):43-73 (2016); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026) [S]</item><item ID="referral-order">Referral to medical oncology, Beatriz Lozano, MD, ordered 1979-03-09 [S]</item></list></text>

